    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 14,
    "summary": "Job testifies of the shortness of life, the certainty of death, and the guarantee of a resurrection—He asks, If a man die, will he live again?—Job answers that he will await the Lord’s call to come forth from the grave.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Man that is born of a woman is of few days, and full of trouble.",
        "footNotes": [
